  "22:11": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "To use Seamless Video Continuation:\n1. Turn it on (scroll down to the below yellow toggles: Enable Seamless Video Continuation).\n2. Load a video.\n3. Select where it begins and ends with the blue bar. The end is where the new gen will begin from.\\n4. Select if the video has Audio or No Audio (important that only 1 is selected, and that selection be correct)\n5. Select either 5, 22, or 39 overlap frames. This is what goes to Minimax as context frames.\n6. Type your prompt here. It can all be natural language, no need for fancy prompting tags like [video editing] or anything. Just describe what happens.\n7. Choose your other video options and then hit the green \"Manual Random Seed\" bottom to the top right of this!\n8. That gens your three 1st pass sample previews. After they're done, right click on the video of one and choose \"Sync Preview\". Then above the sample previews, select which one you like best in the toggle.\n9. To the right of that, turn on Final Upscale pass, and then run the workflow. It will take your selected latent from memory and begin to upscale it.\n\nReminder that a 2.0 upscale multiplier takes a 0.5 MP gen to 2.0 MP, a 4x increase in pixels.  Even 5090's have a hard time with genning 10+ seconds at 2.0 (1080p) size. 0.3 MP -> 1.2 MP upscale is more than enough quality for most purposes!"
    },
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Prompt"
    }
  },
